            {
                "entry_id": "7c2fd908-508f-3645-b6c7-01e88070fce8",
                "word": "loyalist",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "665f08bf-a19e-4649-8441-203f8ecb4ece",
                        "entry_id": "7c2fd908-508f-3645-b6c7-01e88070fce8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "loyalists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                        "entry_id": "7c2fd908-508f-3645-b6c7-01e88070fce8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who is loyal to a cause, generally used as a political affiliation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "16cc0025-369d-48cc-8ea1-42b5650d7c27",
                                "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                                "text": "Most estimates place one-third of Americans as loyalist, one-third on the fence, to be swayed by whomever was winning, and one-third rebel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cef05b4-e41a-48d2-9953-25a03c72c4e0",
                                "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                                "text": "Cobble Hill’s “first hipster bar” sports a “funky living room-ish setting” with “interesting” artwork on the walls and a “low-key” vibe in the air; a “cool” back garden and occasional “dorktastic trivia” contests lead loyalists to label it “one of the best on Atlantic” Avenue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4879b717-12b4-492d-bf54-85d3697d285a",
                                "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                                "text": "In this sense, a new loyalist aesthetic can also be perceived in simplistic works such as anticommunist literature and melancholic works such as nostalgic fiction and prose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db41520d-b686-4ce3-bd77-3e5825638518",
                                "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                                "text": "An obvious characteristic of a kakistocrat is inserting unqualified loyalists into positions of power. Nepotism and kakistocracy go hand-in-hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "834f28de-26a1-48ff-9366-6ccd6cb488a7",
                                "sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                                "text": "President-elect Donald Trump plans to nominate firebrand loyalist Kash Patel to serve as FBI director, an extraordinary move that would put a self-described enemy of the so-called deep state as the head of the nation’s top law enforcement agency — a role that would give Patel power to carry out Trump’s threats to go after his political opponents."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1900f2ee-d71d-4e5a-ac47-3f3182d7e333",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c2fd908-508f-3645-b6c7-01e88070fce8",
                        "source_sense_id": "6b5d9cf7-0412-3172-a5e9-131de3a3d0a2",
                        "source_sense_description": "a person who is loyal to a cause",
                        "target_lang_word": "loyaliste",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loyaliste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad048285-baac-39b2-8131-61a96ea6edd0",
                                        "entry_id": "4416854f-4516-3fef-9006-7f098dad8c4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui a des sentiments de loyalisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bb92e0e-3f94-409f-a4e9-16b7396e4929",
                                                "sense_id": "ad048285-baac-39b2-8131-61a96ea6edd0",
                                                "text": "Un loyaliste pouvait vous tuer s’il vous imaginait complice, un conjuré si vous étiez sur la liste des personnes à éliminer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8c57732-7f90-3da7-86a9-0c2afb73199b",
                                        "entry_id": "4416854f-4516-3fef-9006-7f098dad8c4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Habitant des colonies anglaises ayant déclaré leur indépendance pour fonder les États-Unis resté loyal à la Couronne d'Angleterre et ayant par conséquent déménagé au nord dans ce qui constitue le Canada actuel (principalement en Ontario, au Québec, au Nouveau-Brunswick et en Nouvelle-Écosse)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "475c9bb4-b580-4578-ae98-ab3ee4e16e05",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c57732-7f90-3da7-86a9-0c2afb73199b",
                                                "text": "On établit souvent des parallèles entre les Acadiens et les loyalistes comme éléments fondateurs de la Nouvelle-Écosse et du Nouveau-Brunswick, soit le départ forcé de l'un et l'arrivée forcée de l'autre. On dit aussi que les loyalistes ont repris les anciennes terres des Acadiens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
